From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:59:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(lanes): batch source-owned projection histories [daveey]

The projection visits every open card but queried each event history separately, multiplying SQLite calls under serve GIL contention. Batch up to 400 selected card IDs on first demand, retain only request-local rows, and leave terminal parents lazy. Failed batches publish nothing. Whole-card source choice and per-card event order are preserved; no watcher, timer, new DB handle or cross-request memo is added.

Proof: regression RED at 805 history statements versus 3 and 12 selected-source reads versus 2. GREEN: 91 tests in five lanes consumer files; scripts/check all guards green. This is a bounded read batching improvement, not live latency or CPU acceptance.
